{#
  What is wrong *together*.

  The findings list ranks problems one at a time; this section is the only
  place a document says that three of them form a route. Ordered by hops rather
  than by severity, because a shorter route is both likelier to be walked and
  cheaper to sever — and the line that matters to whoever acts on this report
  is the last one in each block, which names the single link to cut.
#}
<div class="paths">
<h2 class="section-title" id="attack-paths">Attack paths</h2>

{% if not report.attack_paths %}
<p class="muted">
  No route was found from an internet-facing asset to a sensitive one. What
  counts as sensitive is declared per environment in CloudGuard, so an estate
  where nothing has been classified will also report none — this is not by
  itself an all-clear.
</p>
{% else %}
{% if report.fix_plan and report.fix_plan.cuts %}
{# The plan the page leads with (DECISIONS.md section 252): what to change
   first, and what each change closes once the ones before it are made. #}
<div class="card plan">
  <p class="path-route">
    {{ report.fix_plan.cuts | length }} change{{ '' if report.fix_plan.cuts | length == 1 else 's' }}
    close{{ 's' if report.fix_plan.cuts | length == 1 else '' }}
    {% if report.fix_plan.remaining == 0 %}all {{ report.fix_plan.total }}{% else %}{{ report.fix_plan.total - report.fix_plan.remaining }} of {{ report.fix_plan.total }}{% endif %}
    route{{ '' if report.fix_plan.total == 1 else 's' }}
  </p>
  <ol class="steps">
    {% for cut in report.fix_plan.cuts %}
    <li>{{ cut.sentence }} <span class="muted">Closes {{ cut.closes }}, {{ cut.closed_after }} in all.</span></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% if report.fix_plan.remaining %}
  <p class="muted">
    {{ report.fix_plan.remaining }} route{{ '' if report.fix_plan.remaining == 1 else 's' }}
    need{{ 's' if report.fix_plan.remaining == 1 else '' }} changes made together; no single further
    change closes one.
  </p>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endif %}

<p class="lede">
  Each route runs from something reachable to something worth taking. Fewer
  hops is worse: the route is shorter to walk and there are fewer places to
  break it.
</p>

{% for path in report.attack_paths %}
<div class="card path">
  <table class="card-head">
    <tr>
      <td class="path-route">{{ path.entry }} → {{ path.target }}</td>
      <td class="right"><span class="hops">{{ path.hops }} hop{{ '' if path.hops == 1 else 's' }}</span></td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <ol class="steps">
    {% for step in path.steps %}
    <li>{{ step }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% if path.cheapest_break %}
  <p class="cut"><strong>Cut here:</strong> {{ path.cheapest_break }}</p>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
</div>
